  "verdict": "Over 1991–2020 the site cell's hourly ERA5 10 m wind reaches Beaufort 5 (8.0 m/s) on 0.20 h/day in month 01 and 0.03 h/day in month 06: 10 h at Beaufort 5 take ≈ 50 days starting in 01 and ≈ 391 days in 06. With the sheet's set (4 strain sensors and 1 tilt sensor on one receiver, 0.265 A) a 60 Ah battery lasts 9.4 days and a 100 Ah one 15.7, so the best month costs 6 / 4 visits (60 / 100 Ah) and the worst 42 / 25. The all-year 99th percentile of the hourly wind is 7.39 m/s. These are 30-year monthly means; a given winter can give half as much, and how ERA5's open-terrain wind maps to the wind under the canopy is what the campaign measures, not what this assumes."
